<div class="deaths-door-dialog-content">

	{{! The move heads every step of its own walkthrough; "Refuse to Go" and the insert's own
	    questions are past it, and bring their own headings. }}
	{{#unless (or isFate isChoices)}}
	<h2 class="deaths-door-move-name">{{move.name}}</h2>
	<p class="deaths-door-intro deaths-door-move-trigger">{{{move.trigger}}}</p>
	{{/unless}}

	{{#if isRoll}}
	<div class="deaths-door-step deaths-door-step--roll">
		{{! One <span> around the whole run: .deaths-door-note is a flex row, and bare inline
		    text beside the icon would break into an anonymous item per run. }}
		<p class="deaths-door-note">
			<i class="fas fa-feather"></i>
			<span>The Lady of Crows and the Last Door are yours and your table's to describe. They
			might even appear differently for different characters.</span>
		</p>

		{{#if hasStatChoice}}
		{{! The Heavy's Hard to Kill: "you can roll +CON or +nothing (your choice)". The move's
		    name and its own words both come from the owned Item, so a player who is suddenly
		    offered a stat can see which move is giving it to them and read why. }}
		<div class="deaths-door-roll-option">
			<span class="deaths-door-roll-option-label">{{#if statChoiceMove}}{{statChoiceMove}}, {{/if}}roll with:</span>
			<div class="deaths-door-stat-choices">
				{{#each statChoices}}
				{{! The label wraps the radio so the text is a hit target too. No `is-checked`
				    mirror class: the radio's own dot is the state, and the dialog doesn't
				    re-render on change, so a stamped class would go stale on the first click. }}
				<label class="deaths-door-stat-choice-label">
					<input type="radio" class="deaths-door-stat-choice" name="deaths-door-stat"
					       value="{{stat}}" {{#if selected}}checked{{/if}}>
					<span>{{label}}</span>
				</label>
				{{/each}}
			</div>
			{{#if statChoiceMoveDescription}}
			{{! Raw: this is the move's own stored HTML, the same string its card and the playbook
			    reference print. }}
			<div class="deaths-door-roll-option-move">{{{statChoiceMoveDescription}}}</div>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{#if unstoppableMarks}}
		<p class="deaths-door-penalty-note">
			<i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>
			<strong>Unstoppable</strong>: {{penalty}} for {{unstoppableMarks}} circle{{#unless (eq unstoppableMarks 1)}}s{{/unless}} marked.
		</p>
		{{/if}}

		{{! Stakes first, then the roll — which is in the footer with "Not yet", the one place a
		    dialog's actions live. }}
		<div class="deaths-door-outcomes">
			<p class="deaths-door-outcomes-label">However it lands:</p>
			{{> "stonetop.deaths-door-outcomes" tiers=tiers}}
		</div>

		<p class="deaths-door-note">
			<i class="fas fa-hourglass-half"></i>
			<span>No rush: the book lets you hold off until the scene wraps up or the other PCs
			get a little spotlight. "Not yet" closes this and leaves you dying.</span>
		</p>
	</div>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isResult}}
	<div class="deaths-door-step deaths-door-step--result">
		{{#if rolledTotal}}
		<p class="deaths-door-result-banner">You rolled <strong>{{rolledTotal}}</strong>.</p>
		{{/if}}

		{{! The same ladder the roll step previewed, with the tier that landed picked out, so the
		    result is read against what else was on the table. }}
		<div class="deaths-door-outcomes">
			{{> "stonetop.deaths-door-outcomes" tiers=tiers}}
		</div>

		{{#if isStrong}}
		<div class="deaths-door-actions">
			{{#if restored}}
			<p class="deaths-door-applied"><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Back to <strong>1 HP</strong>, and no longer dying.</p>
			{{/if}}

			{{! The mark is already a wound on the sheet by the time this renders (the tier seeds it),
			    so there is no "record" button and no un-recorded state: this is the field where the
			    player says what it was, and it saves itself as they leave it. }}
			<div class="deaths-door-mark">
				<p class="deaths-door-mark-label">Say how it marked you (mind, body, or soul):</p>
				<div class="deaths-door-mark-chips">
					{{#each markChips}}
					<button type="button" class="deaths-door-mark-chip" data-mark="{{this}}">{{this}}</button>
					{{/each}}
				</div>
				<div class="deaths-door-mark-row">
					<input type="text" class="deaths-door-mark-input" value="{{markText}}" placeholder="&hellip;or describe your own mark">
				</div>
				{{#if markSeeded}}
				<p class="deaths-door-mark-done">
					<i class="fas fa-check"></i>
					{{#if markText}}Mark recorded on your sheet. Bring it up often.
					{{else}}The mark is on your sheet already. What you write here names it.{{/if}}
				</p>
				{{/if}}
			</div>
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{#if isWeak}}
		<div class="deaths-door-actions">
			{{#if outOfAction}}
			<p class="deaths-door-applied">
				<i class="fas fa-check"></i> No longer dying. Unconscious, or close enough, until the GM says otherwise, 
				still at 0 HP.
			</p>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if hardToKill}}
			{{! Heavy only: the one route back to 1 HP on a weak hit. }}
			<div class="deaths-door-debility-trade">
				{{#if debilityTraded}}
				<p class="deaths-door-applied"><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Debility marked: you regain <strong>1 HP</strong> and stay on your feet.</p>
				{{else if debilityChoices.length}}
				<p class="deaths-door-mark-label"><strong>Hard to Kill</strong> &mdash; mark a debility of your choice to regain 1 HP:</p>
				<div class="deaths-door-debility-choices">
					{{#each debilityChoices}}
					<button type="button" class="deaths-door-debility-btn" data-debility="{{key}}" title="{{description}}">
						{{name}}
					</button>
					{{/each}}
				</div>
				{{else}}
				<p class="deaths-door-roll-option-hint">
					<strong>Hard to Kill</strong>: all three debilities are already marked, so there's none left to trade.
				</p>
				{{/if}}
			</div>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{#if isMiss}}
		<div class="deaths-door-actions">
			{{#if fateApplied}}
			<p class="deaths-door-applied"><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Your fate is recorded. The GM will take it from here.</p>
			{{else}}
			<div class="deaths-door-fates">
				{{#each fates}}
				<button type="button" class="deaths-door-fate-btn" data-fate="{{key}}">
					<span class="deaths-door-fate-label">{{label}}</span>
					<span class="deaths-door-fate-hint">{{hint}}</span>
				</button>
				{{/each}}
			</div>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}
	</div>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isFate}}
	<div class="deaths-door-step deaths-door-step--fate">
		<h2 class="deaths-door-move-name">Refuse to Go</h2>
		<p class="deaths-door-intro deaths-door-move-trigger">
			The GM will ask why you refuse. Name the person, the task, or the reckoning you will not
			leave behind. That's your Terrible Purpose. Then say which way you stay.
		</p>
		<div class="deaths-door-fates">
			{{#each refusalInserts}}
			<button type="button" class="deaths-door-insert-btn" data-slug="{{slug}}">
				<span class="deaths-door-fate-label">{{name}}</span>
				<span class="deaths-door-fate-hint">{{hint}}</span>
			</button>
			{{/each}}
		</div>
	</div>
	{{/if}}

	{{! The insert is theirs; this is what it asks of them. Nothing here is compulsory — the answers
	    live on the sheet and can be changed there — so Done is always live, however much is still
	    outstanding.

	    Laid out as the shared left-rail sheet (the same .stonetop-guide-* chrome as the
	    first-session guide): one question on screen at a time, with the rail carrying the rest and
	    marking off what has been answered. Stacked, the four ran to a window taller than the
	    screen, and a player scrolling past three lists of the book's prose to reach the fourth had
	    no way of telling how much of it was still asking something of them. }}
	{{#if isChoices}}
	<div class="deaths-door-step deaths-door-step--choices">
		<div class="deaths-door-choices-head">
			<h2 class="deaths-door-move-name">{{insertName}}</h2>
			{{! Told per fate — a Thrall didn't refuse anything, they called something up. }}
			<p class="deaths-door-intro">{{choicesIntro}}</p>
		</div>

		<div class="stonetop-guide-split">
			{{! The rail. One entry per question, ticked as each is settled, so what is left to do is
			    read down the margin instead of scrolled for. }}
			<nav class="stonetop-guide-toc" aria-label="What the {{insertName}} insert asks of you">
				<ol class="stonetop-guide-toc-list">
					{{#each choiceTabs}}
					<li class="stonetop-guide-toc-item{{#if isActive}} is-active{{/if}}{{#if done}} is-answered{{/if}}">
						<button type="button" class="stonetop-guide-toc-btn deaths-door-choice-tab"
						        data-choice-step="{{key}}"{{#if isActive}} aria-current="true"{{/if}}>
							<i class="fas {{icon}} stonetop-guide-toc-icon"></i>
							<span class="stonetop-guide-toc-text">{{label}}</span>
							{{#if done}}<i class="fas fa-check deaths-door-choice-tab-done" aria-label="answered"></i>{{/if}}
						</button>
					</li>
					{{/each}}
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<div class="stonetop-guide-main deaths-door-choices-main">
				{{> "stonetop.post-death-choices" choices=choices}}
				{{! This used to name the button that reopened these questions. There is no such button
				    any more — the Post-Death tab prints the insert's own state — so it points at the
				    tab, and at edit mode, which is now the way to change an answer afterwards. }}
				<p class="deaths-door-note">
					<i class="fas fa-hourglass-half"></i>
					<span>No rush: whatever you leave undecided is waiting on your Post-Death tab, and can be
					answered there in edit mode.</span>
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	{{/if}}

</div>

<div class="deaths-door-dialog-buttons">
	{{#if isRoll}}
	{{! The roll is this step's affirmative action, so it takes the left of the footer (Foundry's
	    order) at full button size, and "Not yet" keeps the right edge. The label carries what is
	    being rolled: with no stat choice on offer there is nothing else on the step that says
	    "+nothing". }}
	<button class="deaths-door-roll-btn is-primary" type="button" title="Roll Death's Door">
		<i class="fas fa-dice-d6"></i>
		<span>Roll {{#if hasStatChoice}}the dice{{else}}+nothing{{/if}}</span>
	</button>
	<button class="deaths-door-cancel-btn" type="button">Not yet</button>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isResult}}
	<button class="deaths-door-close-btn is-primary" type="button">
		<i class="fas fa-check"></i> Done
	</button>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isFate}}
	<button class="deaths-door-cancel-btn" type="button">Cancel</button>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isChoices}}
	{{! `title` because the line is clipped to one row now that it shares the footer with three
	    buttons, and on a Thrall with nothing answered it names four steps. }}
	{{#if outstandingLabel}}<span class="deaths-door-outstanding" title="{{outstandingLabel}}">{{outstandingLabel}}</span>{{/if}}
	{{! Back / Next walk the rail; Done leaves. A wizard keeps its forward action on the right (the
	    one place our dialogs don't put the affirmative first), and Done sits past it because it is
	    the way OUT of the walkthrough rather than the next step of it. }}
	<span class="deaths-door-choices-nav">
		<button class="deaths-door-choice-back" type="button"{{#if atFirstChoice}} disabled{{/if}}>
			<span class="stonetop-nav-arrow stonetop-nav-arrow--back"></span>Back
		</button>
		<button class="deaths-door-choice-next" type="button"{{#if atLastChoice}} disabled{{/if}}>
			Next<span class="stonetop-nav-arrow"></span>
		</button>
		<button class="deaths-door-close-btn is-primary" type="button">
			<i class="fas fa-check"></i> Done
		</button>
	</span>
	{{/if}}
</div>
